---
import DocsLayout from "@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import Code from "@/components/Code.astro";
const snippet0 = `from power_pptx.design import DesignTokens

tokens = DesignTokens.from_dict({
    "palette": {
        "primary": "#0B5CFF",
        "surface": "#FFFFFF",
        "ink": "#0D0D0D",
    },
    "typography": {
        "heading": {"family": "Inter", "size": 44.0},   # float = points
        "body":    {"family": "Inter", "size": 18.0},
    },
    "radii": {"card": 8},
    "spacings": {"gutter": 0.2},
})

# …or from YAML (needs pyyaml) or extracted from an existing .pptx
tokens = DesignTokens.from_yaml("brand.yaml")
tokens = DesignTokens.from_pptx("brand-deck.pptx")`;

const snippet1 = `shape.style(tokens, fill="primary", line="ink", radius="card", shadow="sm")`;

const snippet2 = `from power_pptx.design import Grid, Stack

grid = Grid(slide, rows=2, cols=3, gutter=Inches(0.2), margin=Inches(0.5))
for i, cell in enumerate(grid.cells()):
    slide.shapes.add_text(cell, text=f"Tile {i + 1}", align="center")

stack = Stack.vertical(slide, BBox.from_inches(1, 1, 8, 5), gap=Inches(0.15))
for region in stack:
    ...`;

const snippet3 = `from power_pptx.design.recipes import (
    title_slide, bullet_slide, kpi_slide, quote_slide, image_hero_slide,
)

title_slide(prs, tokens, title="Q4 Review", subtitle="Engineering")
bullet_slide(prs, tokens, title="Highlights", bullets=[...])
kpi_slide(prs, tokens, title="KPIs", kpis=[{"label": "ARR", "value": "$4.2M"}])
quote_slide(prs, tokens, quote="Ship it.", attribution="The team")
image_hero_slide(prs, tokens, image="hero.png", title="Big news")`;

const snippet4 = `from power_pptx import (
    add_kpi_card, add_progress_bar, add_gauge,
    add_status_pill, add_stat_strip, add_article_card,
)

kpi = add_kpi_card(slide, bb, tokens, label="MRR", value="$120k", delta="+8%")
bar = add_progress_bar(slide, bb, tokens, value=0.72, label="Migration")
gauge = add_gauge(slide, bb, tokens, value=0.6)
pill = add_status_pill(slide, bb, tokens, text="On track", tone="success")
strip = add_stat_strip(slide, bb, tokens, stats=[...])
card = add_article_card(slide, bb, tokens, title="…", dek="…")`;

const snippet5 = `from power_pptx import (
    add_plotly_figure, add_matplotlib_figure, add_svg_figure, add_html_figure,
)

add_plotly_figure(slide, bb, fig)          # Plotly → PNG → picture
add_matplotlib_figure(slide, bb, fig)      # Matplotlib → PNG → picture`;

---

<DocsLayout
  title="Design System"
  description="DesignTokens, the shape.style facade, Grid/Stack layout primitives, slide recipes and shape-level building blocks."
>
  <p class="lead">
    The design layer gives generated decks a consistent visual language: tokens for palette,
    typography, shadows, radii and spacing; a token-resolving style facade; geometry-safe layout
    primitives; and opinionated recipes for whole slides.
  </p>

  <h2 id="tokens">DesignTokens</h2>
  <Code code={snippet0} />
  <p>
    <strong>Gotcha:</strong> bare-int sizes in typography are interpreted as EMU, not points — use
    floats (<code>44.0</code>) or <code>Pt(44)</code>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="style">The shape.style facade</h2>
  <Code code={snippet1} />

  <h2 id="layout">Grid and Stack</h2>
  <p>
    Layout primitives compute geometry from the slide's real dimensions, so you can't walk off the
    right edge:
  </p>
  <Code code={snippet2} />

  <h2 id="recipes">Slide recipes</h2>
  <Code code={snippet3} />
  <p>
    Recipes use the Blank layout, so <code>slide.shapes.title</code> is <code>None</code> — address
    shapes by index.
  </p>

  <h2 id="components">Shape-level building blocks</h2>
  <p>
    Token-driven cards that return small dataclasses exposing their constituent shapes for further
    tweaks:
  </p>
  <Code code={snippet4} />

  <h2 id="figures">Figure adapters</h2>
  <Code code={snippet5} />
  <p>
    Third-party deps import lazily; a missing backend raises
    <code>FigureBackendUnavailable</code> naming the exact pip package to install.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
